1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Your business has workflows. You want AI to help run them.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
But sensitive actions must still be approved independently.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:23,000
MCP gives different assistants a shared interface to reusable tools.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Shared MCP tools prepare actions. Our separate service controls
approval.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:41,000
A demo MCP client reads a real public GitHub issue.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Preparing a follow-up creates no task.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The QA reviewer rejects Draft 1. No manual human approval
observed.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Rejected means blocked. The MCP client cannot approve itself.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
A different proposal. A new draft. Still no task.

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The QA reviewer approves Draft 2. No manual human approval
observed.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Approved, not executed. Still zero tasks.

12
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Execution creates one local SQLite task. No ERP or GitHub write.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Retry: same receipt, one local SQLite task. No ERP or GitHub write.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Shared MCP tools. Independent control. A local proof of concept.
